{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.no_contentZero_two_row_at_nuclear_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.no_contentZero_two_row_at_nuclear_level","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L217-L222","doc":"**No isospin-type two-row block at a nuclear level `n = 3A` with `A ≥ 2`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.size_le_four_of_contentDoubled_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.size_le_four_of_contentDoubled_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L211-L215","doc":"A content-zero two-row shape has at most four boxes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentDoubled_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentDoubled_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L198-L209","doc":"**The isospin-type class the row cap admits is `{∅, (1), (2,1), (2,2)}`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentDoubled_pos_of_three_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentDoubled_pos_of_three_le","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L188-L196","doc":"With three or more columns in the first row the content sum is strictly\npositive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentDoubled_neg_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentDoubled_neg_iff","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L163-L174","doc":"**The charge-type class the row cap admits is the singleton `{(1,1)}`.**\nAmong two-row shapes, `c(λ) < 0` holds for `(1,1)` and nothing else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentDoubled_nonneg_of_two_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentDoubled_nonneg_of_two_le","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L153-L161","doc":"With two or more columns in the first row the content sum is already\nnonnegative, because `a(a-1) ≥ 2` outweighs the second row's floor of `-2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.two_le_row_two_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.two_le_row_two_content","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L144-L151","doc":"`b(b-3) ≥ -2` for every natural `b`, since `(b-1)(b-2) ≥ 0` over the\nintegers. This is what stops the second row from ever dragging the content sum\nbelow `-2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentDoubled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentDoubled","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L140-L142","doc":"Twice the content sum of the two-row shape `(a, b)`, kept doubled so the\nstatement stays in `ℤ` with no division: `2·c(a,b) = a(a-1) + b(b-3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.two_two_survives_row_cap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.two_two_survives_row_cap","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L106-L109","doc":"`(2,2)` also has at most two rows, so it survives convention D's row cap —\nthe one self-conjugate shadow price `QOU/Hecke/SelfConjugateRowCap.lean` leaves\nstanding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.charge_class_of_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.charge_class_of_four","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L101-L104","doc":"The charge-type members at level 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.volume_class_of_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.volume_class_of_four","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L97-L99","doc":"The volume-type members at level 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.isospin_class_of_four_is_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.isospin_class_of_four_is_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L91-L95","doc":"**The isospin-type class at level 4 is a singleton.** Among the partitions\nof 4, `c(λ) = 0` holds for `(2,2)` and nothing else — so \"isospin-type at the\nquartet level\" forces the partition with no freedom left to fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentSums_of_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentSums_of_four","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L87-L89","doc":"The content sums, computed. `(2,2)` is the only zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.partitionsOfFour","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.partitionsOfFour","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L82-L85","doc":"The five partitions of 4, in dominance order. Completeness (`p(4) = 5`) is\nthe standard fact, checked in the probe rather than here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentSum","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L79-L80","doc":"`c(λ) = Σ_{(i,j)∈λ} (j - i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentFrom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.contentFrom","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L74-L77","doc":"Content sum from row index `i` downward. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.rowContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IsospinClassSingleton.rowContent","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/IsospinClassSingleton.lean#L69-L72","doc":"Content of one row: row `i` of length `len` contributes\n`Σ_{j < len} (j - i) = len(len-1)/2 - i·len`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}